Native DXVK
-----------
Jk4Speed uses JkFlow's Native DXVK renderer client (d3d9.c988.dll). Our
changes to DXVK in it: Copyright (c) 2026 XxXJoker13XxX. Free to use, copy,
change and redistribute, if every release names the author with the line
"Native DXVK by XxXJoker13XxX". Full terms: LICENSES/Native-DXVK.txt. The
DXVK base stays zlib/libpng (LICENSES/DXVK-zlib.txt).

  [OWNER DECISION] Whether the source of the Jk4Speed changes to the
  client is published (JkFlow 1.00 did not publish the Native DXVK source).

Third-party components
----------------------
Third-party components keep their own licences. See THIRD_PARTY.md for the
list and LICENSES/ for the full texts:
  - Wine and the Wine-based PS4 runtime: LGPL-2.1-or-later. Where to get
    the source: SOURCES.txt.
  - DXVK: zlib/libpng
  - Mesa / RADV: MIT
Xidi (BSD-3-Clause) and Fusion Fix (GPL-3.0) are not part of Jk4Speed; the
README links to them.

Jk4Speed contains no files from Electronic Arts. Need for Speed and Need
for Speed: Most Wanted are trademarks of Electronic Arts. The game is not
included; you use your own copy. This is an unofficial fan project.
